; A holding moved between two accounts, with no money in the entry.
;
; Transferring shares in kind — one broker to another, or a taxable account to
; a registered one — is two postings in the same security and nothing else. No
; posting states a rate and no posting is in a currency, so the two rules that
; pick what the entry is denominated in have nothing to answer with, and the
; only candidate left is the security itself.
;
; GnuCash takes that in memory and does not keep it: measured, the transaction
; read back denominated in the book's own currency after a save, leaving the
; 10 units valued as 10 dollars — a figure with no source in the file. Its own
; register records such a transfer with what the units are worth on it, so
; that is what this asks for. beancount_shares_moved_with_a_value.beancount is
; the same transfer, stated.
;
; What this fixture produces: a refusal naming the security and saying a
; transaction is kept in a currency.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
    gnucash-mnemonic: "CAD"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Canadian Dollar"
    gnucash-fraction: "100"
2024-01-01 commodity NASDAQ.HOOL
    gnucash-mnemonic: "HOOL"
    gnucash-namespace: "NASDAQ"
    gnucash-fullname: "Hooli Inc"
    gnucash-fraction: "1"
